        "title": "A Profound and Spiritual Experience at Pashupatinath",
        "text": "Pashupatinath Temple offers a profound glimpse into Nepal’s spiritual and cultural traditions. The open-air cremations along the Bagmati River are intense yet deeply meaningful, reflecting Hindu beliefs on life and rebirth. The evening aarati is mesmerizing, with fire rituals, chanting, and devotion filling the air.\n\nSadhus, with their striking appearances, and pilgrims from across the region add to the temple’s unique atmosphere.\n\nPro Tip:\n\nWear a mask—smoke and incense can be overwhelming.\n\nRespect traditions—photography is restricted in certain areas.\n\nEntry fee applies—only Hindus can enter the main temple.\n\nA visit to Pashupatinath is a moving and unforgettable experience.\n\n",
