        "title": "Hindu temple with traditional cremation ceremonies. A world heritage site. ",
        "text": "This world heritage site is the closest to the airport and largest of the seven I visited in the Kathmandu and surrounding areas. It's also different as cremation ceremonies are happening by the water live. I was with a local board of tourism friend who explained the process, site, and beliefs; as these might be very different from culture to culture. You can watch the cremation ceremonies from different parts of the site and as close as you wish to be. It's a different experience I had not witnessed before. ",
